{"review_id":"00001788285779241470-0002412995-000003-cycle-review-1","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:0e95e96401eadde223f78d4ed89c98bed283b836226d3d585b2345fbdd4f4077","findings":[{"finding_id":"F1-truncate-panic","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"run-command output truncation can panic on a non-char-boundary","claim":"`SandboxedToolExecutor::run_command` builds `combined` from `read_to_string` stdout/stderr (valid UTF-8, possibly multi-byte) and then calls `combined.truncate(self.max_output_bytes)` whenever the output exceeds the limit. `String::truncate` panics if `new_len` does not fall on a UTF-8 char boundary, so any tool command that emits enough output to cross `max_output_bytes` with a multi-byte character straddling that byte index will panic the executor thread instead of returning a truncated result.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":314,"end":320}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:1afb2b6456989bee8096f975351afa347236cee45c214afbe93aad0ea7a0ffa0","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":32355,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788282372975203-0002412995-000000/PRD-58","revision":"sha256:68465d347edc7f9f96a1b1f5a9d249cecbcf6e62ba693f403c3edc668d2fd3d2","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-1afb2b6456989bee8096f975351afa347236cee45c214afbe93aad0ea7a0ffa0-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Truncate on a char boundary instead of a raw byte index — e.g. compute a safe boundary with `combined.floor_char_boundary(self.max_output_bytes)` (or iterate `char_indices`) before truncating, or operate on bytes with `String::from_utf8_lossy`. No existing test exercises multi-byte output over the limit, so add one.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F2-context-ceiling-unenforced","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Configured max_context_tokens ceiling is never enforced by the loop","claim":"`AgentRuntimeCeilingsConfig` defines and documents `max_context_tokens` (also surfaced in config/default.toml) as a ceiling, but the loop's `LoopCeilings` struct carries only `max_iterations`, `max_output_tokens`, and `max_wall_clock_ms`, and `run_loop` never checks any context-token total. The value is silently ignored, so acceptance criterion 'iteration, token, and context ceilings are enforced preemptively' is not met for the context dimension — an operator who sets `max_context_tokens` gets no context-window protection.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":82,"end":86}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/raw_runtime.rs","range":{"start":1,"end":1306}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:1afb2b6456989bee8096f975351afa347236cee45c214afbe93aad0ea7a0ffa0","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":32355,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788282372975203-0002412995-000000/PRD-58","revision":"sha256:68465d347edc7f9f96a1b1f5a9d249cecbcf6e62ba693f403c3edc668d2fd3d2","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-1afb2b6456989bee8096f975351afa347236cee45c214afbe93aad0ea7a0ffa0-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Either add a `max_context_tokens` field to `LoopCeilings` and enforce it preemptively before each submission (breaking with `StopReason::TokenOrContextCeiling` when the accumulated context total would exceed it), or, if context enforcement is deferred to a later phase, remove/clearly document `max_context_tokens` as inert so the config does not imply a protection that does not exist.","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
